  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000095949,
      "SummaryText": "As of June 2, 2025 the facility ID 100000195013 located at 216 Brookhollow Industrial BLVD Dalton Ga. will transfer from Cargill Inc. to the new owner Aditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc.\n\nAccidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies:\n\nAditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc is committed to providing the necessary resources to ensure the safe handling of Epichlorohydrin to prevent accident releases of Epichlorohydrin by having appropriate safeguards (process safety information, process hazardous analysis, operating procedures, management of change, hot work procedures, mechanical integrity program, employee training, etc.) in place.  In the event of an emergency, Aditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc is committed to providing the resources necessary to report, contain and cleanup accidental releases of Epichlorohydrin in a manner that minimizes the adverse impacts to its on-site personnel as well as to the surrounding community / environment.\n\nFacility Description and Regulated Substances Handled:\nAditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc will acquire the Cargill inc. Dalton, GA facility on June 2, 2025. The facility uses Epichlorohydrin to produce numerous epoxy additives.  Aditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc will receive Epichlorohydrin via tanker trucks and store up to 156,800 lbs of Epichlorohydrin in an above ground storage tank.\n\nGeneral Accidental Release Prevention Program and Chemical Specific Prevention Steps:\nAditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc has developed its Epichlorohydrin chemical release prevention program based upon the requirements of USEPA's Risk Management Program (RMP) and OSHA's Process Safety Management (PSM) regulations.\n\nFive Year Accident History:\nDuring the past five years, no accidents involving the accidental release of epichlorohydrin have resulted in any on-site deaths, injuries, or significant property damage or any known off-site deaths, injuries, evacuations, sheltering in place, property damage or environmental damage.\n\nEmergency Response Pro"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000095949,
      "SummaryText": "gram:\nAditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc trains its employees initially (and annually thereafter) on its Emergency Action Plan and how to recognize / report emergencies to the appropriate facility personnel and government agencies. Emergency response activities have also been coordinated with the Dalton Fire Department and Whitfield County LEPC.  Additionally, Aditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc has retained a Hazmat emergency response organization (Clean Harbors) to provide emergency hazmat spill containment and remediation services.\n\nPlanned Changes to Improve Safety:\nAfter taking ownership of the Dalton, GA Cargill inc.  facility, Aditya Birla Chemicals (USA) Inc will conduct a Process Hazard Analysis (PHA) of the epichlorohydrin process before the end of CY 2025.  Any corrective actions identified by the PHA will be resolved in a timely manner."
    }
  ]
